  "_comment": "Every test in every suite has exactly one testing type, so any type can be run on its own across all four suites: `make test-type TYPE=negative`. Python suites (api, judge, sdk) apply these rules at collection time as pytest markers (-m negative); the browser suite carries the same names as Playwright tags (--grep @negative). Rules are fnmatch patterns on the test id WITHOUT parameters, first match wins, so put specific patterns before a file's catch-all. `make check-types` fails if any test matches no rule. Agreed with the product owner 2026-09-28.",
  "types": {
    "positive": "The happy path works: valid input gives the right, KB-correct result.",
    "negative": "Invalid input, misuse or out-of-scope questions are refused, and wrong answers are caught.",
    "edge": "Boundaries and odd shapes: formats, ranges, timing, memory, interruptions, parser corner cases.",
    "security": "Auth and tokens, tampering, prompt injection, unsafe requests, data that must never leak or reach a real person.",
